**By.linkText() - Exact Match for Links**
**By.partialLinkText() - Partial Match for Links**

Both work ONLY with `<a>` anchor tags (links).

**By.linkText() - Exact Match:**
```java
// HTML: <a href="/login">Click here to login</a>

// ✅ Correct - Exact text match
WebElement loginLink = driver.findElement(By.linkText("Click here to login"));

// ❌ Wrong - Partial text fails
driver.findElement(By.linkText("login")); // NoSuchElementException!
```

**By.partialLinkText() - Partial Match:**
```java
// HTML: <a href="/login">Click here to login</a>

// ✅ All of these work
WebElement link1 = driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("login"));
WebElement link2 = driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("Click here"));
WebElement link3 = driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("to login"));
```

**Comparison:**

| Feature | linkText() | partialLinkText() |
|---------|------------|-------------------|
| **Match Type** | Exact full text | Partial/substring |
| **Case Sensitive** | Yes | Yes |
| **Flexibility** | Low | High |
| **Precision** | High | Low |
| **Best For** | Short, stable text | Long or dynamic text |

**Real-World Examples:**

```java
public class LinkLocators {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
        driver.get("https://example.com");

        // Exact match
        driver.findElement(By.linkText("Contact Us")).click();
        driver.navigate().back();

        // Partial match - useful for dynamic text
        // HTML: <a>Welcome back, John Smith!</a>
        driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("Welcome back")).click();
        driver.navigate().back();

        // Partial match - long text
        // HTML: <a>Click here to view all products in our catalog</a>
        driver.findElement(By.partialLinkText("view all products")).click();

        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

**When to Use Each:**

**Use linkText():**
- Short, stable link text
- Exact text match needed
- More precise/reliable

**Use partialLinkText():**
- Long link text (partial matching is easier)
- Link text has dynamic content ("Welcome, UserName")
- Link text may change slightly
- Don't know exact full text

**Important Notes:**
⚠️ Both are CASE SENSITIVE
⚠️ Work ONLY with `<a>` tags (not buttons or other elements)
⚠️ Spaces matter in exact match

**By.cssSelector() - Powerful and Flexible**

CSS Selectors use CSS syntax to locate elements. More powerful than basic locators.

**Basic Patterns:**

**1. By ID:** `#id-value`
```java
// HTML: <input id="username">
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#username"));
// Equivalent to: By.id("username")
```

**2. By Class:** `.class-name`
```java
// HTML: <button class="btn-primary">Submit</button>
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(".btn-primary"));
// Equivalent to: By.className("btn-primary")
```

**3. By Tag:** `tagname`
```java
// HTML: <h1>Title</h1>
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("h1"));
// Equivalent to: By.tagName("h1")
```

**4. By Attribute:** `[attribute='value']`
```java
// HTML: <input type="email" name="user-email">
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("[type='email']"));
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("[name='user-email']"));
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("input[type='email']"));
```

**Advanced Patterns:**

**5. Multiple Classes:** `.class1.class2`
```java
// HTML: <div class="error message">Error!</div>
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector(".error.message"));
```

**6. Descendant (space):** `parent descendant`
```java
// HTML: <div id="form"><input name="email"></div>
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#form input"));
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("div#form input[name='email']"));
```

**7. Direct Child (>):** `parent > child`
```java
// HTML: <div id="container"><ul><li>Item</li></ul></div>
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#container > ul"));
```

**8. Attribute Contains:** `[attribute*='value']`
```java
// HTML: <a href="https://example.com/page">Link</a>
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("a[href*='example']"));
```

**9. Attribute Starts With:** `[attribute^='value']`
```java
// HTML: <input id="user_email">
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("[id^='user']"));
```

**10. Attribute Ends With:** `[attribute$='value']`
```java
// HTML: <input id="confirm_email">
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("[id$='email']"));
```

**11. nth-child:** `:nth-child(n)`
```java
// Get 3rd list item
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("ul li:nth-child(3)"));

// Get first item
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("ul li:first-child"));

// Get last item
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("ul li:last-child"));
```

**Complete Example:**
```java
public class CssSelectorExamples {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
        driver.get("https://example.com");

        // ID
        driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#username")).sendKeys("user");

        // Class
