**By.xpath() - Most Powerful Locator**

XPath (XML Path Language) can navigate through any element in the DOM.

**Two Types:**
1. **Absolute XPath** - Full path from root (Brittle, NOT recommended)
2. **Relative XPath** - Starts from anywhere (Flexible, RECOMMENDED)

**Basic Syntax:**

**1. Absolute XPath (❌ Avoid):**
```java
// Starts from root, breaks easily
driver.findElement(By.xpath("/html/body/div[1]/form/input[2]"));
```

**2. Relative XPath (✅ Use This):**
```java
// Starts with //, flexible
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='username']"));
```

**Common XPath Patterns:**

**1. By Attribute:**
```java
// Single attribute
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='username']"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[@class='submit-btn']"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//a[@href='/logout']"));
```

**2. By Text:**
```java
// Exact text
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[text()='Submit']"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//a[text()='Click Here']"));

// Contains text
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[contains(text(),'Submit')]"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//p[contains(text(),'Welcome')]"));
```

**3. Multiple Attributes (AND):**
```java
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@type='text' and @name='email']"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[@class='btn' and @type='submit']"));
```

**4. Multiple Attributes (OR):**
```java
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='email' or @name='email']"));
```

**5. Contains Attribute:**
```java
// Attribute contains value
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[contains(@id,'user')]"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//a[contains(@href,'logout')]"));
```

**6. Starts With:**
```java
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[starts-with(@id,'user')]"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//div[starts-with(@class,'error')]"));
```

**7. Parent/Child Navigation:**
```java
// Direct child: /
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//div[@id='form']/input"));

// Any descendant: //
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//div[@id='container']//input"));

// Parent: ..
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='email']/.."));
```

**8. Following/Preceding Siblings:**
```java
// Following sibling
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//label[@for='email']/following-sibling::input"));

// Preceding sibling
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='password']/preceding-sibling::label"));
```

**9. Index (Position):**
```java
// First input
driver.findElement(By.xpath("(//input)[1]"));

// Last input
driver.findElement(By.xpath("(//input)[last()]"));

// Third button
driver.findElement(By.xpath("(//button)[3]"));
```

**10. Not (Negation):**
```java
// Input that is NOT hidden
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[not(@type='hidden')]"));
```

**Complete Example:**
```java
public class XPathExamples {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
        driver.get("https://example.com/login");

        // By attribute
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='username']")).sendKeys("user@test.com");

        // By text
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[text()='Login']")).click();

        // Contains text
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//p[contains(text(),'Welcome')]"));

        // Multiple attributes
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@type='password' and @name='pwd']")).sendKeys("pass");

        // Parent-child
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//div[@class='form-group']//input[@type='text']"));

        // Following sibling
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//label[text()='Email']/following-sibling::input"));

        // Contains attribute
        driver.findElement(By.xpath("//button[contains(@class,'submit')]")).click();

        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

**XPath Axes (Advanced):**
```java
// ancestor
"//input[@id='email']/ancestor::form"

// descendant
"//form/descendant::input"

// following
"//label[@for='email']/following::input[1]"

// preceding
"//button[@id='submit']/preceding::input[2]"

// parent
"//input[@id='email']/parent::div"
```

**Advantages:**
✅ Most powerful and flexible
✅ Can locate any element
✅ Can navigate relationships (parent, sibling, child)
✅ Can use text content
✅ Can use complex conditions

**Disadvantages:**
❌ Slower than CSS Selector
❌ More complex syntax
❌ Can be brittle if not written carefully

**Best Practices:**
- Use relative XPath (//), not absolute (/html/body...)
- Keep XPath simple and readable
- Use attributes instead of text when possible
- Avoid complex nested paths
- Test XPath in browser console: $x("//input[@id='username']")

