**Common Locator Errors & Solutions**

**1. NoSuchElementException**
```
org.openqa.selenium.NoSuchElementException: 
no such element: Unable to locate element
```

**Causes:**
- Element doesn't exist on page
- Wrong locator
- Element not loaded yet
- Element in iframe
- Typo in locator

**Solutions:**
```java
// ✅ Add wait
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement element = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.id("username")));

// ✅ Check if element exists
List<WebElement> elements = driver.findElements(By.id("username"));
if (!elements.isEmpty()) {
    elements.get(0).click();
}

// ✅ Verify locator in browser console
// $$("#username") or $x("//input[@id='username']")
```

**2. StaleElementReferenceException**
```
org.openqa.selenium.StaleElementReferenceException:
stale element reference: element is not attached to the page document
```

**Cause:** Element was found, but DOM refreshed/changed

**Solution:**
```java
// ❌ Bad - Element becomes stale after page refresh
WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("item"));
driver.navigate().refresh();
element.click(); // Stale!

// ✅ Good - Re-find element after refresh
driver.navigate().refresh();
WebElement element = driver.findElement(By.id("item"));
element.click();
```

**3. InvalidSelectorException**
```
org.openqa.selenium.InvalidSelectorException:
invalid selector
```

**Causes:**
- Syntax error in CSS/XPath
- Invalid characters
- Incomplete selector

**Solutions:**
```java
// ❌ Bad - Syntax errors
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#username password")); // Missing dot or #
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='username'"))  ; // Missing ]

// ✅ Good - Correct syntax
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#username"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//input[@id='username']"));

// Test selector in console first!
```

**4. ElementNotInteractableException**
```
org.openqa.selenium.ElementNotInteractableException:
element not interactable
```

**Causes:**
- Element hidden (display: none)
- Element covered by another element
- Element not clickable yet

**Solutions:**
```java
// ✅ Wait for element to be clickable
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement element = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id("submit")));
element.click();

// ✅ Scroll to element
JavaScriptExecutor js = (JavaScriptExecutor) driver;
js.executeScript("arguments[0].scrollIntoView(true);", element);
element.click();
```

**5. TimeoutException**
```
org.openqa.selenium.TimeoutException:
Expected condition failed: waiting for visibility of element
```

**Causes:**
- Element takes longer than timeout
- Element never appears
- Wrong expected condition

**Solutions:**
```java
// ✅ Increase timeout
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(30));

// ✅ Use correct condition
// Use presenceOfElementLocated for hidden elements
wait.until(ExpectedConditions.presenceOfElementLocated(By.id("hidden")));

// Use visibilityOfElementLocated for visible elements
wait.until(ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.id("visible")));
```

**6. Multiple Elements Found (Wrong Element Clicked)**

**Problem:**
```java
// ❌ Multiple buttons with class "btn", clicks first one
driver.findElement(By.className("btn")).click(); // Might click wrong button!
```

**Solutions:**
```java
// ✅ Use more specific locator
driver.findElement(By.id("submit-btn")).click();

// ✅ Use findElements and select correct one
List<WebElement> buttons = driver.findElements(By.className("btn"));
buttons.get(2).click(); // Click 3rd button

// ✅ Combine with parent
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("#loginForm .btn")).click();
```

**7. Dynamic Element Not Found**

**Problem:** Element ID/class changes on each page load

**Solutions:**
```java
// ❌ Bad - Dynamic ID
// HTML: <div id="panel-1234-abcd">
driver.findElement(By.id("panel-1234-abcd"));

// ✅ Good - Partial match
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("[id^='panel']")); // Starts with
driver.findElement(By.cssSelector("[id*='panel']")); // Contains
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//div[starts-with(@id,'panel')]"));
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//div[contains(@id,'panel')]"));
```

